WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
 It's crazy. Finally, I was able to support fully

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.760
 transparent videos in fframes.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.680
 This situation with transparent video is ridiculously

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.760
 bad on the web and basically anything supports

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:18.220
 it correctly. It's madness. WebM, VP9 codec with

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:22.000
 transparency mode, does not actually behave

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.970
 like it is a transparency mode just stores the alpha

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:29.200
 channel separately. There is hevc (h265)

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.590
 with support for the alpha channel which doesn't work

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.760
 either because you need a specific build

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.510
 of hevc encoder to actually have support of the alpha

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:40.800
 channel. There is Apple ProRes which actually

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:45.000
 supports alpha channel correctly but it is

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.400
Apple's vendor-locked codec and basically it is a nightmare and

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.160
 surprisingly fframes already supports them all

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:58.160
 out of the box and just works fine. I am SUPER excited


